摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Google Antigravity (agy) OAuth auth + model access plugin for DeepSeek Harness: multi-account pool, 429 rotation, device fingerprinting, CLI and web login.","id":"gh:1334109809","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-agy","slug":"chaos-03x/dsh-agy","topics":["agy","antigravity","claude","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","gemini"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Google Antigravity (agy) OAuth auth + model access plugin for DeepSeek Harness: multi-account pool, "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"429 rotation, device fingerprinting, CLI and web login."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-agy"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Google Antigravity (agy) access for DeepSeek Harness:\nOAuth authentication, a multi-account pool wit"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"h automatic 429 rotation, device\nfingerprinting, and both CLI and web management."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> 中文文档：docs/README_zh.md"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **OAuth login**: one-click sign-in via browser OAuth callback, with headless\npaste-URL mode and a "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"remote paste-credential blob channel.\n- **Two management surfaces**: web and CLI, either one works, "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"core features are\nthe same.\n- **Multi-account pool**: encrypted account store, usage-aware account\ns"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"election (family-scoped quotas, OMP-aligned ranking), automatic rotation on\nrate limits, per-account"},{"id":"p6s5","text":" cooldown to the real reset time, per-account device\nfingerprints.\n- **Inline Settings UI**: an Anti"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"gravity section inside DSH Settings with five\ntabs — accounts (login, activation, grouped 5-hour/wee"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"kly quota windows, test\ncalls, fingerprint and proxy management), models (per-model visibility), con"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"fig\n(thinking budgets, multimodal inline limit), usage (cumulative token and request\nstatistics), an"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"d credentials (import/export).\nNo separate page: the surface only exists where DSH Settings does.\n- "},{"id":"p6s10","text":"**Quota badge in the session header**: the tightest of the active account's\ntracked windows (5-hour "},{"id":"p6s11","text":"vs weekly) as a single figure, with the per-window\nbreakdown and reset walls on hover. It reads the "},{"id":"p6s12","text":"same grouped quota windows the\nSettings section shows, so the header and the panel cannot disagree.\n"},{"id":"p6s13","text":"- **Model visibility toggles**: hide individual models from the DSH model\nselector. Blacklist semant"},{"id":"p6s14","text":"ics — only models you switch off are hidden, so\nmodels the server adds later stay visible.\n- **Usage"},{"id":"p6s15","text":" statistics**: input / output / cache-read / cache-write tokens,\nrequest counts, failures, rate limi"},{"id":"p6s16","text":"ts, rotations, latency and\ntime-to-first-token, aggregated by account and by model. Includes calls t"},{"id":"p6s17","text":"hat\nnever pass through DSH (CLI, verification, test calls), which no\nsession-based statistic can see"},{"id":"p6s18","text":".\n- **CLI**: `dsh-agy login|status|import|verify|logout` works standalone, with or\nwithout a harness"},{"id":"p6s19","text":"\n- **CLI**: `dsh-agy login|status|import|verify|logout` works standalone, with or\nwithout a harness."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The Antigravity section inside DSH Settings. Account emails and project names are\nredacted."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Accounts | Models |\n|:---:|:---:|"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| **Limits** — 5-hour and weekly windows | **Usage** — cumulative, per-model and per-account |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Quickstart"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Path A: DSH Web GUI Users (Recommended — 100% Web UI, zero CLI commands)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"For users using DeepSeek Harness browser workspace / Web GUI:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The section lives in **Settings → Antigravity** (top-level, alongside General\nand Models). There is "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"no separate dashboard page: the old `/agy` URL is gone."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Path B: Headless / Terminal Only (Standalone CLI)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"For Linux VPS, SSH remote servers, or headless CI environments:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## CLI reference"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Command | Options | Description |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| `dsh-agy login` | `--headless` — print the auth URL and wait for a pasted redirect URL\n`--blob` — "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"print a paste-credential blob instead of storing the account\n`--port <n>` — loopback callback port ("},{"id":"p21s3","text":"default `51121`)\n`--project <id>` — bind the login to a specific project\n`--timeout <ms>` — callback"},{"id":"p21s4","text":" timeout (default `300000`) | Interactive Google OAuth |\n| `dsh-agy status` | — | List accounts + pe"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"r-model quota summary |\n| `dsh-agy import <files...>` | `--blob` — the pasted value is a credential "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"blob\n`--email <email>` — set the account email (skips userinfo verification)\n`--overwrite` — replace"},{"id":"p21s7","text":" an existing account with the same email | Import agy auth.json files or credential blobs (multiple "},{"id":"p21s8","text":"files / multi-line paste = batch import) |\n| `dsh-agy export` | `--index <n>` — export one account b"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"y index (default: all)\n`--out <dir>` — write one `dsh-agy-<index>.blob` per account (default: print "},{"id":"p21s10","text":"to stdout, one blob per line) | Export account credentials as paste blobs |\n| `dsh-agy verify` | `--"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"index <n>` — verify one account by index (default: all) | Refresh + health check |\n| `dsh-agy health"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"` | `--index <n...>` — check only these accounts (default: all enabled)\n`--interval <ms>` — repeat o"},{"id":"p21s13","text":"n an interval instead of once | Batch health check (refresh + userinfo), re-enables accounts whose c"},{"id":"p21s14","text":"redentials are live again |\n| `dsh-agy logout` | `--index <n>` — account index (default: active)\n`--"},{"id":"p21s15","text":"email <email>` — account email | Remove an account |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Path C: Local Development & Link"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Requires Node >= 22."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### About cache hits: why not 99% like DeepSeek V4?"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Bottom line: the cache hit strategy is decided by the model provider's cache\nmechanics (for us, Anti"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"gravity's); agy's mechanics differ from DeepSeek's in\ntwo ways, so its hit rate is naturally a notch"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"mechanics differ from DeepSeek's in\ntwo ways, so its hit rate is naturally a notch below DeepSeek's."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"**First, the entry threshold.** DeepSeek's caching is on by default with no\nthreshold — its very fir"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"st request already hits a previously cached system\nprompt. agy's Gemini-tiered models only start cac"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"hing once the request prefix\nreaches roughly 16k tokens, while DSH's default bare system prompt is o"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"nly\nabout 13k — below the line. So every new conversation's first 1-2 requests\nare 0%, until the acc"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"umulated messages pass 16k."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**Second, how fast the cache updates.** DeepSeek refreshes its cache at the\nend of every request — o"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"nly the newest message misses each round, giving\nnear-100%. agy's cache updates lag: this round's ad"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ditions are not hit in\nthe next round — they enter the cache roughly two rounds later, and requests\n"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"for the same content in between all count as misses. Every round wastes\nabout 1.5-2× its additions; "},{"id":"p28s5","text":"the long-conversation hit rate keeps rising as\nthe context grows, bounded by the model's context win"},{"id":"p28s6","text":"long-conversation hit rate keeps rising as\nthe context grows, bounded by the model's context window."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"**Practical tips**"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- Don't expect 99% from agy: the gap comes from upstream mechanics, with no\nroom to optimize.\n- If y"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ou have a weird number obsession, stuff some custom content into the\nSystem Prompt (MCP / tool defin"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"itions / roleplay ...)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
